            <h4 style="color: #002147; border-bottom: 2px solid #004080; padding-bottom: 5px; font-size:20px; font-weight:600;">About Dr. Nitish Jauhari</h4>
            <p style="font-size:16px; font-family:Arial; line-height:30px; text-align:justify; color:black;">
                Dr. Nitish Jauhari is working as an Assistant Professor in the Department of Civil Engineering at Bharat Ratna Babasaheb Bhimrao Ambedkar Rajkiya Engineering College, Pratapgarh. Currently, he is serving as the Co-ordinator of Institution’s Innovation Council at  Bharat Ratna Babasaheb Bhimrao Ambedkar Rajkiya Engineering College, Pratapgarh. His research interest includes, Geotechnical Engineering, Ground Improvement and Computational Geotechnics. He has obtained his Ph.D. from Indian Institute of Technology Patna in 2025.   Before Ph.D, he has worked as Assistant Professor in the Department of Civil Engineering at Rajshree Institute of Management and Technology, Bareilly for three years. He has completed his M. Tech from Govind Ballabh Pant University of Agriculture and Technology, Pantnagar and B. Tech from Dr. APJ Abdul Kalam Technical University, Lucknow. Dr. Nitish has published more than 20 research papers in reputed International/national journals and conferences. He is a life member of Indian Geotechnical Society.  He is also a recipient of Young Geotechnical Engineer Award-2024, presented by Indian Geotechnical Society.
            </p>

